{"base_rate":0.29958960328317374,"brier":0.11895389876880984,"bss":0.43310926530393834,"bss_hi":0.518930040569913,"bss_lo":0.36423913360846233,"chart":{"base":[321.0,126.3],"fp":[302.6,265.0],"lead":"62,225.5 272,191.9 482,144.3 692,64.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 83% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +10pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 22% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 3%; promised 93% → rained 83%"},"rel":"62,453.2 103.5,396.2 321,282.5 650.4,107.5"},"country":"RO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.056456908344733284,"ess":395.4817617619809,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Bacau</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Bacau rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>87%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 731 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-30. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBACAU, 3.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 37 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(15&ndash;70) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>271</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>105</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>87%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Bacau</b> <span class=\"muted\">Romania</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;30% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 30% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>15&ndash;70\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>731 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Bacau &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Bacau\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.62,352.64516129032256 88.81485714285715,330.0 152.89166666666665,245.5 252.84351351351356,140.97297297297297 365.37314285714285,38.80000000000001 409.7932467532469,18.0 409.7932467532469,27.45454545454544 365.37314285714285,96.0 252.84351351351356,224.59459459459458 152.89166666666665,321.3333333333333 88.81485714285715,368.1333333333333 68.62,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"272.9493844049248\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"272.9493844049248\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,371.2546125461255 68.62,352.64516129032256 88.81485714285715,305.73333333333335 152.89166666666665,275.8333333333333 252.84351351351356,180.32432432432432 365.37314285714285,96.0 409.7932467532469,65.27272727272731\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 271 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"371.2546125461255\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.62\" cy=\"352.64516129032256\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 105 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"88.81485714285715\" cy=\"305.73333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 27%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"152.89166666666665\" cy=\"275.8333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 55%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"252.84351351351356\" cy=\"180.32432432432432\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 87%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"365.37314285714285\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.7932467532469\" cy=\"65.27272727272731\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Bacau the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.34).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>155</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.343</td><td class='num'>3.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.384</td><td class='num'>7.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.401</td><td class='num'>8.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.578</td><td class='num'>4.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":46.56718,"lon":26.91384,"n":731,"n_cities":216,"name":"Bacau","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":271,"obs":0.02952029520295203,"sig":true},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.030000000000000002,"n":62,"obs":0.08064516129032258,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.08704761904761905,"n":105,"obs":0.20952380952380953,"sig":true},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.26805555555555555,"n":72,"obs":0.2916666666666667,"sig":false},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.5504054054054055,"n":74,"obs":0.5540540540540541,"sig":false},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.8682857142857143,"n":70,"obs":0.7857142857142857,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9937662337662341,"n":77,"obs":0.8701298701298701,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.8,"provisional":false,"rank":37,"rank_hi":70.0,"rank_lo":15.0,"reliability":0.00501455135510822,"resolution":0.09574964717891549,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"bacau","station":"BACAU","timezone":"Europe/Bucharest"}